{
  "requirement": "Saved configuration MUST remain distinct from resolved runtime configuration.\nSerializing and deserializing a valid configuration MUST preserve its semantic\nvalues, including explicit versus omitted settings. Optional fields MAY be\nomitted on serialization; defaults and environment-derived values MUST NOT be\nmaterialized into omitted fields. TOML comments and formatting need not\nround-trip.\n\nLoading configuration or running a configured feature MUST NOT rewrite the user\nor project configuration as a side effect. Resolved credentials and live runtime\nobjects MUST NOT enter the serialized data structures. Explicitly supplied\ncredential values are permitted only in the fields documented by the authoring\nfeature; credentials resolved from a profile or environment MUST NOT be written\nback to configuration.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the implementation and tests satisfy `requirements.configuration.serialization`.** I found a few marking nits, listed at the end, but no behavioural gap.\n\n**Implementation** (all in `src/config.rs`)\n\n- **Saved versus resolved configuration.**\n  - The serde types (`UserConfig`, `WorkspaceConfig`, `AuthoringConfig`, `BedrockConfig`, `OllamaConfig`, and so on) hold only saved values.\n  - Resolved runtime values are produced separately. `OllamaConfig::api_key_from` returns a plain `String` from the environment lookup and stores it nowhere. `resolve_authoring_with_workspace_from` returns a `ResolvedAuthoringConfig` that is not `Serialize`. It copies the saved `concurrency` (still `None` when omitted) and the cloned backend.\n  - No resolved credential or live runtime object is stored in any serialized type.\n  - `endpoint` stays `Option<String>`. The default is applied only in `endpoint()`, not stored.\n  - Both `api_key` and `api_key_env` are separate optional fields, so an environment name is saved but the environment value never is.\n- **Semantic round trip and omitted optionals.**\n  - Every optional field uses `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = ...)]`, so omitted fields are not materialized.\n  - Explicit values serialize normally, including `SecretString` (`#[serde(transparent)]`) for explicit credentials.\n  - `UserAuthoringConfig.configs` is required but may be empty, which preserves the explicit empty table.\n  - `to_toml` validates before it serializes, and `parse` / `load_*` validate on decode.\n- **No rewrite as a side effect.** `load_user_config`, `load_workspace_config`, `workspace_document`, `parse_document`, and `resolve_authoring*` only read. Nothing in `src` writes user or workspace configuration. The only config-adjacent writer is the explicit `setup` command, which edits `book.toml`. It is not a load or a configured-feature run.\n- **Credentials.** Explicit credentials are accepted only in the documented fields: `BedrockConfig.credentials` and `OllamaConfig.api_key`. `validate` rejects conflicting combinations of explicit credentials with a profile or an environment name.\n\n**Tests** (`tests/configuration.rs`)\n\n- `absent_and_minimal_configuration_are_distinct_and_read_only`: absent versus minimal config, the file and its comment are unchanged after loading, and the result round-trips.\n- `backend_configuration_round_trips_without_materializing_defaults`: no `endpoint` or `concurrency` appears in the output, arbitrary nested options are preserved, and the result round-trips.\n- `authoring_concurrency_defaults_overrides_and_invalid_values`: an omitted `concurrency` stays omitted on serialization while the effective default is only computed at resolution, and an explicit value round-trips.\n- `ollama_authentication_resolves_separately_and_rejects_missing_values`: the environment variable name is serialized but the resolved value is not.\n- `explicit_credentials_round_trip_but_diagnostics_and_debug_redact_them`: explicit credentials round-trip for both backends, and the invalid forms (conflicting, empty, wrong type) are rejected.\n- `workspace_discovery_uses_nearest_file_without_merging_or_rewriting_it`: the file on disk is unchanged after load, an omitted `configs` stays omitted, and the result round-trips.\n- `user_and_workspace_authoring_tables_round_trip_every_map`: projects, an empty `configs`, workspace configs, and options all round-trip.\n- `workspace_defaults_and_configs_combine_with_existing_user_selections`: resolution across user and workspace files does not merge or alter the saved records.\n\n**Minor observations, not gaps**\n\n- The `Serialize` structs (for example `OllamaConfig`, `BedrockConfig`, and `EvidenceConfig`) carry the `skip_serializing_if` behaviour. They are marked `{impl}` for `authoring.configuration_serialization`, `authoring.configuration_structure`, or `configuration.evidence_paths`, not for this requirement. Their text carries out this part. `authoring.configuration_serialization` explicitly says to follow the common rules in this requirement, and the shared round-trip behaviour is tested.\n- `load_workspace_evidence` and `resolve_authoring` also only read, but they are not marked for this requirement. The \"no rewrite\" obligation is met by the absence of any writer, so this is a labelling nit only.\n- Explicitly empty optional collections (`options = {}` or `configs = {}` in a workspace file) serialize as omitted. The spec defines omitted as empty, and the values are equal, so semantics are preserved.",
